commit 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
Author: libpg_query <noreply@libpg_query>
Date:   Thu May 21 00:00:00 2026 +0000

    PL/pgSQL: Add byte-offset location info to all statement and variable nodes

    Adds an `int location` field to every PL/pgSQL statement struct
    (PLpgSQL_stmt_* types), to PLpgSQL_exception, PLpgSQL_if_elsif,
    PLpgSQL_case_when, and the four variable types (PLpgSQL_var,
    PLpgSQL_row, PLpgSQL_rec, PLpgSQL_recfield).  The field is populated
    in the grammar actions (pl_gram.y) by assigning the bison location
    token (@N) immediately after the existing lineno assignment.

    This allows callers of pg_query_parse_plpgsql() to obtain exact byte
    offsets for each statement or variable declaration, which is needed
    for accurate source-location reporting.

